  "faqBudgetingQ": "How does envelope budgeting work?",
  "@faqBudgetingQ": {
    "description": "FAQ question"
  },
  "faqBudgetingA": "You give all the money you have a job: assign it to categories until To Be Budgeted is zero. You spend from what a category has available. If you overspend, move money from another category to cover it.",
  "@faqBudgetingA": {
    "description": "FAQ answer"
  },
  "faqSafeQ": "Is my data safe?",
  "@faqSafeQ": {
    "description": "FAQ question"
  },
  "faqSafeA": "Your data is stored only on your phone, in an encrypted database whose key is kept in the phone’s secure hardware (Android KeyStore). The app lock adds your fingerprint, face or phone PIN. Synced data is encrypted before it leaves the phone. There are no LedgerZero servers, no tracking and no analytics.",
  "@faqSafeA": {
    "description": "FAQ answer"
  },
  "faqSyncQ": "How do my partner and I share a budget?",
  "@faqSyncQ": {
    "description": "FAQ question"
  },
  "faqSyncA": "Open Settings > Sync Settings. At home, pair the phones over Wi-Fi by scanning a QR code. To sync while you are apart, both phones use the same Google Drive account and sync passphrase. The user guide chapter “Using LedgerZero with a partner” explains the details.",
  "@faqSyncA": {
    "description": "FAQ answer"
  },
  "faqOfflineQ": "Can I use the app offline?",
  "@faqOfflineQ": {
    "description": "FAQ question"
  },
  "faqOfflineA": "Yes. Everything works offline. Sync catches up automatically when you are back online.",
  "@faqOfflineA": {
    "description": "FAQ answer"
  },
  "faqBackupQ": "How do backups work?",
  "@faqBackupQ": {
    "description": "FAQ question"
  },
  "faqBackupA": "Settings > Backup & Export creates a backup file that is always encrypted with a backup password you choose. Without that password the backup cannot be restored. CSV and JSON exports are readable copies and are not encrypted.",
  "@faqBackupA": {
    "description": "FAQ answer; menu names must match the settings labels"
  },
  "faqImportQ": "Can I import from YNAB or my bank?",
  "@faqImportQ": {
    "description": "FAQ question"
  },
  "faqImportA": "Yes. Settings > YNAB Migration imports nYNAB CSV exports and YNAB 4 budgets. Settings > Import CSV reads the CSV export of your bank.",
  "@faqImportA": {
    "description": "FAQ answer; menu names must match the settings labels"
  },
  "guideStartTitle": "Getting started",
  "@guideStartTitle": {
    "description": "User guide chapter title"
  },
  "guideStartBody": "LedgerZero uses envelope budgeting: before you spend money, you give it a job by budgeting it to a category. Add the account your money is in, add your salary, then budget until To Be Budgeted is zero. The ⓘ buttons across the app explain each part where you need it.",
  "@guideStartBody": {
    "description": "User guide chapter text"
  },
  "guideAccountsTitle": "Accounts",
  "@guideAccountsTitle": {
    "description": "User guide chapter title"
  },
  "guideAccountsBody": "Add every account with its current balance. Accounts in the budget (checking, cash, credit cards) hold the money you budget. Savings, brokerage and pension accounts usually stay outside the budget: they count towards net worth only. The type sets the icon and whether a new account starts in the budget.",
  "@guideAccountsBody": {
    "description": "User guide chapter text"
  },
  "guideBudgetTitle": "Budgeting",
  "@guideBudgetTitle": {
    "description": "User guide chapter title"
  },
  "guideBudgetBody": "On the Budget screen, tap a category’s budgeted amount to give it money, until To Be Budgeted is zero. Income without a category adds to To Be Budgeted; add your salary as recurring income to see what is coming. Each category keeps what is left from month to month. A new month starts empty: fill it like the month before or from a template, by hand or automatically. Money left unbudgeted at the end of a month is offered for savings in the next one.",
  "@guideBudgetBody": {
    "description": "User guide chapter text"
  },
  "guideTransactionsTitle": "Transactions",
  "@guideTransactionsTitle": {
    "description": "User guide chapter title"
  },
  "guideTransactionsBody": "Record each expense with a payee and a category; it reduces what the category has available. Quick Add lets you type a transaction in one line, rules categorise transactions automatically, and with card notifications on, payments from your bank app arrive as transactions to approve.",
  "@guideTransactionsBody": {
    "description": "User guide chapter text"
  },
  "guideOverspendingTitle": "Overspending",
  "@guideOverspendingTitle": {
    "description": "User guide chapter title"
  },
  "guideOverspendingBody": "When a category's available amount turns red, you have spent more than you budgeted. Move money from another category to cover it.",
  "@guideOverspendingBody": {
    "description": "User guide section text"
  },
  "guideReconcileTitle": "Reconciling",
  "@guideReconcileTitle": {
    "description": "User guide chapter title"
  },
  "guideReconcileBody": "Now and then, compare an account with your bank statement using Reconcile Account on the account screen. Cleared transactions are marked as reconciled, and any difference is recorded as an adjustment.",
  "@guideReconcileBody": {
    "description": "User guide section text"
  },
